{"step_index":421,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T19:57:10Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-11T01:57:10+06:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T01:57:10+06:00\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/User/.gemini/antigravity/brain/216e255d-b8e0-4484-815a-117107eae7cd/walkthrough.md`\nTotal Lines: 167\nTotal Bytes: 9075\nShowing lines 1 to 100\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # Walkthrough: MedCheck BD Platform\n2: \n3: **MedCheck BD** is a full-stack, Bangladesh-focused medicine verification, price transparency, availability tracking, and pharmacy management web platform connecting **Customer → Pharmacy → Admin**.\n4: \n5: ## Project Location & Status\n6: - **Directory**: `C:\\Users\\User\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\medcheck-bd`\n7: - **Port**: `5000` (Accessible at `http://localhost:5000`)\n8: - **Database**: Live MongoDB connection (`mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/medcheck_bd`) with automated `mongodb-memory-server` fallback for zero-configuration execution.\n9: - **Dataset**: Pre-seeded with 22 realistic Bangladeshi medicines (Beximco, Square, Incepta, Renata, Opsonin), 47 batches, 10 pharmacies across Dhaka and major divisions, live inventory, and demo user accounts.\n10: \n11: ---\n12: \n13: ## What Was Built\n14: \n15: ```\n16: medcheck-bd/\n17: ├── client/\n18: │   ├── index.html                 # Public Landing Page & Healthcare Workflow\n19: │   ├── login.html                 # 1-Click Multi-Role Demo Login\n20: │   ├── register.html              # Customer Registration\n21: │   ├── pharmacy-register.html     # Pharmacy Onboarding with License\n22: │   ├── verify.html                # Medicine & Batch Verification\n23: │   ├── medicine-details.html      # Comprehensive Regulatory Profile\n24: │   ├── price.html                 # Price Check & DGDA Variance Engine\n25: │   ├── pharmacies.html            # Verified Pharmacy Directory\n26: │   ├─\n<truncated 3151 bytes>\nsplaying DGDA license, operating hours, and live inventory table with status pills (`IN STOCK`, `LOW STOCK`, `OUT OF STOCK`, `EXPIRED`).\n72: \n73: ### 4. Pharmacy Dashboard & POS Terminal (`pharmacy-dashboard.html`)\n74: - Real-time stock counts with automated alerts for:\n75:   - Low Stock (< 10 units)\n76:   - Expiring Soon (< 60 days)\n77:   - Expired batches\n78: - Inventory CRUD modal (Add, Edit price/quantity, Delete).\n79: - Point-of-Sale (POS) modal: Dispenses medicines, deducts inventory automatically, links customer phone to purchase history, and generates a verifiable **Digital Receipt**.\n80: \n81: ### 5. Printable Digital Receipt (`receipt.html`)\n82: - Unique receipt ID format: `MC-2026-XXXXXX`.\n83: - Itemized breakdown, pharmacy details, payment mode (Cash, bKash, Nagad, Card), subtotal, discount, barcode simulation, and clean `@media print` layout.\n84: \n85: ### 6. Customer Hub & Medicine History (`customer-dashboard.html`, `history.html`)\n86: - Personal ledger of verified medicines and purchases.\n87: - Quick action shortcuts (Verify, Compare, Find, Report).\n88: - History filters (All, Verifications, Purchases) and clear/delete actions.\n89: \n90: ### 7. Administrative Oversight & Analytics (`admin-dashboard.html`)\n91: - **Chart.js Visualizations**:\n92:   - Reports by issue category (Counterfeit, Expired, Wrong Price, etc.).\n93:   - Pharmacies by division/area.\n94:   - Medicines by therapeutic class.\n95: - **1-Click Pharmacy Approval**: Inspect pending applications and grant the `VERIFIED PHARMACY ✓` badge.\n96: - **Medicine Database Manager**: Add, edit, or remove medicines from central registry.\n97: - **Suspicious Reports Review**: Update report status (Investigating, Resolved, Dismissed).\n98: - **Security Access Audit Stream**: Real-time logging of sensitive actions with timestamps, user role, and IP address.\n99: \n100: ---\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
